# Lint and auto-fix staged files before each commit.
#
# Call the local binary directly instead of `npx`: Node's global npx shim
# (`C:\Program Files\nodejs\npx`) is a `#!/usr/bin/env bash` script, and on
# Windows hosts where `bash` resolves to the WSL launcher
# (C:\Windows\System32\bash.exe) with no usable distro, the hook dies with
# "execvp(/bin/bash) failed: No such file or directory". husky's `h` wrapper
# already puts `node_modules/.bin` on PATH, and npm's local shims there use
# a plain `#!/bin/sh` shebang — no bash involved.
lint-staged
